  areas={[
    { href: '/boiler-service-liverpool', label: 'Liverpool' },
    { href: '/boiler-service-st-helens', label: 'St Helens' },
    { href: '/boiler-service-formby', label: 'Formby' },
  ]}
  related={[
    { href: '/gas-safety-certificate-wirral', title: 'Gas safety certificate Wirral', text: 'Landlord CP12 £75, or £195 with a service' },
    { href: '/boiler-installation-wirral', title: 'Boiler installation Wirral', text: 'Fixed-price combi packages from £2,195 fitted' },
    { href: '/power-flushing-wirral', title: 'Power flushing Wirral', text: 'Cold radiators and sludge, from £395' },
    { href: '/hot-water-cylinders-wirral', title: 'Hot water cylinders Wirral', text: 'Replacements and unvented servicing' },
    { href: '/radiators-wirral', title: 'Radiators Wirral', text: 'New radiators supplied and fitted from £245' },
    { href: '/emergency-plumber-wirral', title: 'Emergency plumber Wirral', text: 'From £120 for the first hour, no call-out fee' },
  ]}
  finalTitle="Book your Wirral boiler service"
  finalText="£95 including VAT. No call-out fee. Every CH postcode. Service record emailed the same day."
  serviceName="Boiler Service Wirral"
  serviceType="Annual gas boiler service"
  serviceDesc="Annual gas boiler servicing across the Wirral, CH41 to CH64, by Gas Safe registered engineers. Combi, system and regular boilers. Benchmark service record emailed the same day."
  areaServed={['Wirral', 'Birkenhead', 'Wallasey', 'New Brighton', 'Moreton', 'Prenton', 'Oxton', 'Hoylake', 'West Kirby', 'Heswall', 'Pensby', 'Bebington', 'Bromborough', 'Neston']}
>
  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="local">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What does your Wirral home need from a boiler service?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Every service covers the same full checklist. But Wirral homes vary a lot, so we focus on different things in different parts of the peninsula.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Birkenhead, Wallasey and Rock Ferry (CH41, CH42, CH44)</h3>
          <p>Lots of older boilers, many fitted before 2005. Old heat exchangers can crack or corrode without any sign. Our flue gas test shows if the boiler still burns gas cleanly. We also check old flue seals in the terraces, as many flues date from the 1990s.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Hoylake and West Kirby (CH47, CH48)</h3>
          <p>Salt air off the Irish Sea speeds up rust on anything outside. We check the flue terminal on the outside wall for rust and blockages. We also check the condensate pipe and any overflow pipes. A boiler can run fine with a corroded flue, so this matters.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Heswall, Pensby and Neston (CH60, CH61, CH64)</h3>
          <p>Bigger homes here often have a system boiler with a hot water cylinder, and more than one heating zone. We check the pump, zone valves, expansion vessel and cylinder thermostat too. It takes longer, but the price stays at £95.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Prenton, Moreton, Bebington and Bromborough (CH43, CH46, CH62, CH63)</h3>
          <p>Mostly semis from the 1980s to 2010s, with combi boilers. Inhibitor is the key check here. It wears out each year. When it runs low, sludge starts to build up. We test it on every service and top it up if it is low.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>Not sure what boiler you have? Tell us the make and model when you call, or send a photo of the front.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="checks">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>What does a boiler service include?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">We take the cover off, clean and check the parts inside, and test that the boiler burns gas safely. Here is the full list.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Safety checks</h3>
          <ul class="sg-ticks">
            <li>Flue gas analysis, to prove the boiler burns gas cleanly</li>
            <li>Gas pressure and gas rate checked</li>
            <li>The flue checked along its route, including the terminal outside</li>
            <li>Safety devices tested, so the boiler shuts down if it should</li>
            <li>Air supply and ventilation checked</li>
            <li>Your carbon monoxide alarm tested, if you have one</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Inside the boiler</h3>
          <ul class="sg-ticks">
            <li>Burner and heat exchanger checked and cleaned</li>
            <li>Condensate trap cleaned, and the condensate pipe checked</li>
            <li>Seals and gaskets checked for wear</li>
            <li>System pressure and expansion vessel checked</li>
            <li>Inhibitor level checked and topped up if low</li>
            <li>Magnetic filter cleaned, if you have one</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
      <h3>System boilers also get</h3>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>Pump and zone valves checked</li>
        <li>Cylinder thermostat and controls tested</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To finish, we run the heating and hot water, fill in the Benchmark record and email you a copy the same day.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="how">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>How does the visit work?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">You book a time, we service the boiler in about an hour, and you get the record by email the same day.</p>
      <ol class="sg-steps">
        <li><strong>Book (2 minutes).</strong> Call or <a href="/get-started">book online</a>. Tell us if you have a system boiler or a cylinder, so we allow enough time.</li>
        <li><strong>We arrive.</strong> A Gas Safe registered engineer comes at the agreed time. Anyone can let us in. You can ask to see the Gas Safe card.</li>
        <li><strong>The service (45 to 75 minutes).</strong> We work through the full checklist. We use dust sheets and tidy up after.</li>
        <li><strong>What we found.</strong> We tell you how the boiler is doing. If something needs fixing, you get a price first. You decide.</li>
        <li><strong>Your record.</strong> We fill in the Benchmark record and email you a copy the same day.</li>
        <li><strong>Next year.</strong> We send a free reminder when the next service is due.</li>
      </ol>
      <div class="brx-cta">
        <p><strong>Boiler due a service on the Wirral?</strong> Call and we will find you the next free slot.</p>
        <a href={TEL} class="brx-btn">Call {PHONE}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="landlords">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Do you do boiler services for Wirral landlords?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. Book the boiler service and gas safety certificate (CP12) together for £195. It saves you £20 and one visit for your tenant.</p>
      <p>The Wirral has one of the biggest rental markets in Merseyside. Most of it is in Birkenhead CH41, Wallasey CH44, Bromborough CH62 and Bebington CH63.</p>
      <p>By law, landlords must have every gas appliance they supply checked every 12 months. Tenants must get a copy of the certificate within 28 days. The rules come from the <a href="https://www.hse.gov.uk/gas/landlords/index.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Gas Safety (Installation and Use) Regulations 1998</a>.</p>
      <div class="brx-table-wrap">
        <table class="brx-table">
          <thead><tr><th></th><th>Boiler service</th><th>Gas safety certificate (CP12)</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><strong>What it does</strong></td><td>Cleans, tests and sets up the boiler</td><td>Checks every gas appliance is safe</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Needed by law?</strong></td><td>No, but most warranties need it</td><td>Yes, for landlords, every 12 months</td></tr>
            <tr><td><strong>Price</strong></td><td>£95</td><td>£75</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>We can arrange access with your tenant or letting agent. See our <a href="/gas-safety-certificate-wirral">Wirral gas safety certificate</a> page for more. The <a href="https://www.nrla.org.uk/resources/looking-after-your-property/landlords-gas-safety-responsibilities" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NRLA</a> also has a useful guide for landlords.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="warranty">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Will a service keep my boiler warranty valid?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">Yes. Most boiler makers want a service every 12 months by a Gas Safe registered engineer, written in the Benchmark record. We do both on every visit.</p>
      <p>Your boiler came with a Benchmark checklist. It is usually in the back of the manual. Each service goes into it. If the boiler breaks down under warranty, the maker can ask to see it. Miss a year and they can refuse a claim.</p>
      <div class="brx-note"><p><strong>Tip:</strong> keep each service within 12 months of the last one. Our free reminder helps you stay on time.</p></div>
      <p>We service all the main makes, including Worcester Bosch, Vaillant, Ideal, Baxi, Glow-worm and Potterton.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec" id="signs">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Does your boiler need a check now?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">If you see any of these signs, do not wait for the yearly service. Call us and we will take a look.</p>
      <ul class="sg-ticks">
        <li>The boiler keeps locking out or showing an error code.</li>
        <li>The pressure keeps dropping, and you keep topping it up.</li>
        <li>Banging, gurgling or whistling noises.</li>
        <li>Black marks or soot around the boiler.</li>
        <li>It has been more than 12 months since the last service.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="brx-danger"><p><strong>Yellow or orange flame, or a carbon monoxide alarm going off?</strong> Turn the boiler off if you can, open the windows and get everyone outside. Call the National Gas Emergency Service on <a href="tel:0800111999">0800 111 999</a> first. Then ring us.</p></div>
      <p>If the boiler has stopped working, you need a repair, not a service. Call our <a href="/emergency-plumber-wirral">emergency plumber on the Wirral</a>. If it is old and keeps failing, see <a href="/boiler-installation-wirral">new boilers on the Wirral</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="brx-sec brx-tint" id="wirral">
    <div class="brx-wrap">
      <h2>Where on the Wirral do you service boilers?</h2>
      <p class="brx-answer">The whole peninsula, CH41 to CH64. The price is the same in every postcode.</p>
      <div class="sg-cols">
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>Birkenhead and central</h3>
          <p>Birkenhead CH41, Rock Ferry and Tranmere CH42, Prenton and Oxton CH43.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>North Wirral</h3>
          <p>Wallasey CH44, New Brighton CH45, Moreton and Leasowe CH46.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>West Wirral</h3>
          <p>Hoylake and Meols CH47, West Kirby and Caldy CH48.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="sg-box">
          <h3>South Wirral</h3>
          <p>Heswall CH60, Pensby CH61, Bromborough and Eastham CH62, Bebington CH63, Neston CH64.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ServiceGuide>
